// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Installation of WSL Kali-Linux
// Sigma ID: eca8ae39-5c3c-4321-b538-9e64fe25822e
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-10-10 | Modified: 2026-11-22
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects installation of Kali Linux distribution through Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL).
//   Attackers may use Kali Linux WSL to leverage its penetration testing tools and capabilities for
//   malicious purposes.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate installation or usage of Kali Linux WSL by administrators or security teams
// References:
//   - https://medium.com/@redfanatic7/running-kali-linux-on-windows-51ad95166e6e
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/3ffc99b34d2dcb4477f5be4ac4a97c03309c9538/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wsl_kali_linux_installation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\wsl.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wsl.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " --install " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -i ") and ProcessCommandLine contains "kali"
